WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:44.279 --> 00:00:45.560
My parents were gypsies.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.439
They lived in a camp like this.

00:00:49.759 --> 00:00:51.159
They named me Davar.

00:00:52.639 --> 00:00:55.720
I travel India entertaining villages
with my monkeys.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:03.880
Shankar is a 15 year old male.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:08.760
His wife Gauri is 16
and never leaves Elama, their baby, alone.

00:01:13.879 --> 00:01:15.519
Elama was born in March.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.440
All monkeys are born in March.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.599
His mother watches him constantly
and lets no one approach him

00:01:23.639 --> 00:01:25.080
except me, of course.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:26.760
I adore the baby.

00:01:32.839 --> 00:01:37.279
It is a true family,
and me, I guess I'm the grandfather

00:01:40.879 --> 00:01:42.040
The monkeys have a kingdom,

00:01:42.599 --> 00:01:43.440
Kishkindah,

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:45.639
a distant place hidden in the mountains.

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:48.919
In a few days,
we will arrive in this legendary country

00:01:49.199 --> 00:01:52.279
that I've been told of
and been dreaming of since my childhood.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.039
Kishkindah has been
the kingdom of monkeys

00:02:39.119 --> 00:02:40.639
since the beginning of time

00:02:40.919 --> 00:02:43.839
and Hanuman, the monkey god,
its king.

00:02:46.559 --> 00:02:50.119
Gauri, Elama, Shankar and I
travel mostly by foot.

00:02:50.199 --> 00:02:52.160
From time to time
we take the train.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:55.559
The conductors do not make us pay
as we amuse the passengers.

00:03:12.639 --> 00:03:15.479
My companions
do not enjoy the bustle of the cities,

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:18.039
so I always pass through them quickly.

00:03:21.759 --> 00:03:24.880
My family has been living with monkeys
for generations,

00:03:25.039 --> 00:03:27.960
as others have with snakes,
bears or elephants.

00:03:28.119 --> 00:03:31.399
It is a tradition that is handed down
from father to son.

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:34.600
My ancestors were very poor.

00:03:35.039 --> 00:03:37.240
They begged door to door
with their monkeys.

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:39.880
All that changed with my uncle Mamu.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:43.119
He was the first to teach his monkeys
a bag of tricks

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:46.679
that left entire villages
laughing long after they had gone.

00:03:50.839 --> 00:03:52.559
Mamu was a great man.

00:03:53.039 --> 00:03:55.240
He taught me to speak with monkeys.

00:03:55.679 --> 00:03:58.600
Because of him,
our family escaped poverty.

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:02.639
After several months of work
with my monkeys,

00:04:03.039 --> 00:04:05.600
we developed a show
that is very successful.

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:08.240
Everyone is waiting for us
before we arrive in a village.

00:04:19.239 --> 00:04:21.720
Shankar is a great comedian
and he loves to make

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:22.880
the audience laugh.

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:25.679
At the sound of my voice,
he knows it is time to start.

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:27.480
I beat my drum.

00:04:27.959 --> 00:04:29.000
Shankar hears it.

00:04:29.679 --> 00:04:31.359
The spectacle begins.

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:23.239
My monkeys
often keep coins for themselves.

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:24.760
Always the shiniest.

00:07:25.559 --> 00:07:27.959
When we pass a shop,
they trade them for a banana

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:29.079
or a piece of cake.

00:07:31.679 --> 00:07:33.519
There are monkeys all over India.

00:07:33.959 --> 00:07:36.200
They live in the forests, in the fields,

00:07:36.279 --> 00:07:38.359
and even come
and steal the food in the cities.

00:07:40.519 --> 00:07:43.480
But their roots are in Kishkindah,
the city of monkeys.

00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:47.119
Over there the rivers, the lakes,
the forest, the fruit trees

00:07:47.239 --> 00:07:48.839
and the mountains
belong to them.

00:07:49.119 --> 00:07:51.079
The monkeys protect their kingdom.

00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:53.320
This realm extends
beyond the river.

00:08:00.119 --> 00:08:01.559
My monkeys feel vulnerable.

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:03.359
The trees are too far away.

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:07.160
I have lived with them
since they were babies.

00:08:07.279 --> 00:08:11.279
Before that, I had two other monkeys
my father had given me when I was 15.

00:08:11.359 --> 00:08:12.920
We were together for 30 years.

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:14.519
I buried them when they died.

00:08:16.279 --> 00:08:20.160
One hears stories of Kishkindah
and the memories of the few people

00:08:20.279 --> 00:08:22.720
who have been there
are filled with strange dreams.

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:29.559
The doors of the kingdom
are on the other side of the river.

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:32.200
I have been told
that the gates are guarded,

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:33.840
but I don't know what that means.

00:09:21.719 --> 00:09:23.440
Here is the entrance of the kingdom.

00:09:24.520 --> 00:09:28.640
Legend says that humans who adventure
here have visions of their previous life.

00:09:31.479 --> 00:09:33.119
Could it be that I was a monkey?

00:11:42.280 --> 00:11:44.000
Hanuman is the monkey god.

00:11:44.599 --> 00:11:48.359
Rama and Sita are the divine couple
most admired by Hindus.

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:50.200
Hanuman is devoted to them,

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:51.359
and in his kingdom,

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:54.080
men follow the example
of the monkey god.

00:12:37.359 --> 00:12:40.719
In this temple,
ten girls and two families of monkeys

00:12:40.840 --> 00:12:44.080
share their food
and peaceful existence next to Lake Pompa.

00:12:45.640 --> 00:12:48.880
They believe that the bottom of the lake
is at the center of the Earth

00:12:48.919 --> 00:12:51.559
and dates
from when humans were still gods.

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:06.400
I feel that my monkeys believe
they are human.

00:13:07.320 --> 00:13:09.039
When they see themselves in a mirror,

00:13:09.119 --> 00:13:10.039
they go crazy.

00:13:10.359 --> 00:13:14.239
They can't imagine that they resemble
the wild monkeys we often encounter.

00:14:33.559 --> 00:14:35.280
I make my monkeys work every day.

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:36.960
I teach them new tricks.

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:39.640
It takes them a month
to learn a new routine.

00:14:59.840 --> 00:15:01.520
Shankar loves to challenge me.

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:04.880
He watches me with his eyes
and tries to apply his law.

00:15:05.799 --> 00:15:06.880
It doesn't work.

00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:08.919
I'm the boss and he knows it.

00:15:09.719 --> 00:15:12.719
When the rehearsal is finished,
Shankar, without being asked,

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:14.479
performs his favorite trick.

00:15:43.919 --> 00:15:45.919
Monkeys have extraordinary vision.

00:15:46.719 --> 00:15:48.679
Shankar adores pictures.

00:15:48.760 --> 00:15:50.440
He examines every detail,

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:55.039
and I often feel
he noticies things I can't see.

00:16:48.799 --> 00:16:51.919
Shankar, Gauri, and I
always sleep under the stars.

00:16:53.599 --> 00:16:55.080
I lay down on the ground,

00:16:55.799 --> 00:16:57.000
but they prefer height.

00:16:58.239 --> 00:17:00.200
They fear panthers and tigers.

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:13.280
One night, my monkeys sensed a panther
prowling under the tree

00:17:13.359 --> 00:17:14.479
they were perched in.

00:17:15.439 --> 00:17:18.280
They were terrified
and escaped from branch to branch.

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:22.880
At dawn, I found them at the centre
of the nearest village.

00:17:22.959 --> 00:17:25.199
They had sought refuge
with human beings.

00:17:33.119 --> 00:17:35.199
I share all my meals with them.

00:17:35.760 --> 00:17:38.079
They eat fruits, vegetables and rice.

00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:43.680
Monkeys have sacs in their cheeks
where they can store entire meals.

00:17:44.520 --> 00:17:47.560
They eat quickly
because they are afraid of missing food.

00:18:36.239 --> 00:18:37.760
We take a bath every morning.

00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:40.000
Shankar swims like an otter.

00:18:40.119 --> 00:18:42.199
But Gauri and Elama don't like water.

00:18:43.199 --> 00:18:46.520
Soon Gauri will be pregnant again
and she will have a daughter.

00:18:47.199 --> 00:18:51.520
Gauri is a possessive mother
and will guard Elama as long as possible

00:18:51.599 --> 00:18:54.359
until a new baby arrives
and fills her days.

00:18:54.719 --> 00:18:59.000
The newborn will become Elama's wife
and they will create a new family.

00:19:45.680 --> 00:19:49.760
Not far from here is the heart
of the kingdom, the birthplace of Hanuman.

00:19:50.760 --> 00:19:53.439
It is a mountain
that has the shape of a monkey's head.

00:19:55.520 --> 00:19:58.520
100 monkeys
and a handful of men live atop it.

00:19:59.520 --> 00:20:01.479
Men who worship the monkey god.

00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:05.199
Men who understand the monkey language.

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:59.359
To come here with my monkeys
is the most beautiful voyage

00:20:59.400 --> 00:21:00.920
I could ever dream about.

00:21:07.640 --> 00:21:10.160
There, the monkey
who loved humans, was born

00:21:10.560 --> 00:21:13.000
the great monkey
with extraordinary powers.

00:21:13.439 --> 00:21:16.160
There some men are celebrating
his existence.

00:22:21.839 --> 00:22:23.839
These men are fascinated by monkeys.

00:22:24.280 --> 00:22:27.800
They know the story of Hanuman
by heart and talk only about it.

00:22:28.160 --> 00:22:30.719
The monkeys living around the temple
hear their stories,

00:22:30.880 --> 00:22:32.800
and seem to respond to their words.

00:22:51.800 --> 00:22:55.119
There was once a great battle here
between two monkey kings.

00:22:55.560 --> 00:22:57.560
A story no one has ever forgotten.

00:22:57.920 --> 00:23:00.839
It was the time
when the war divided the monkey people.

00:24:38.079 --> 00:24:40.479
The men of this country
followed many paths

00:24:40.599 --> 00:24:42.560
to rid themselves of earthly sorrow.

00:24:46.040 --> 00:24:47.640
I have found my path:

00:24:48.800 --> 00:24:50.119
live with my monkeys,

00:24:51.199 --> 00:24:52.280
watch them grow,

00:24:53.119 --> 00:24:54.079
protect them

00:24:55.199 --> 00:24:56.239
love them.

00:24:58.680 --> 00:24:59.560
That's all.

